Package: treetable
Title: Configurable Hierarchical Tree Tables as an 'htmlwidgets' Widget
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Luis Angel", "Casas", , "luisangelcasasbl@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Aggregate a flat data frame into an arbitrary-depth hierarchy
    (group > subgroup > item > ...) with subtotals at every level, and
    render it as an interactive, expandable/collapsible tree table built on
    'htmlwidgets'. Columns can compare one or two metrics side by side (with
    automatic percentage variance), row colors and column number formats are
    fully configurable from R, and each leaf row can open a detail modal
    backed by a table or a user-supplied 'Shiny' UI. Works the same way
    inside and outside 'Shiny' (console, 'R Markdown'/'Quarto', 'Shiny' apps).
